    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Divergent boundaries create new oceanic crust at mid-ocean ridges through constructive volcanic activity.",
        "Convergent boundaries result in crustal destruction, deep-sea trenches, fold mountains, and deep-focus earthquakes.",
        "Transform boundaries slide past each other laterally, generating conservative shear strain and shallow-focus earthquakes.",
        "The point within Earth where seismic energy originates is the focus (hypocenter), whereas the surface point directly above it is the epicenter."
      ],
      "id": "i7qfudo"
    },
    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Differentiate between Focus (underground point of origin) and Epicenter (surface location directly above the focus).",
        "P-waves can travel through solid, liquid, and gas, while S-waves travel exclusively through solids.",
        "Deep-focus earthquakes (Benioff zones) are exclusively associated with convergent plate subduction zones."
